# All values here are FINAL — they replace whatever factions contribute.
# The JSONL is the single source of truth for the StarterForest landscape.
#
# Five quantum axes:
#   Q0: sun/moon   — Day/night (Celestial Archons driver, 50s wall cycle)
#   Q1: wolf/deer  — Predator/prey (Pack Lords, 15s Rabi)
#   Q2: eagle/rabbit — Apex scarcity (eagle pop ~4%, 65s Rabi)
#   Q3: seedling/tree — Growth lifecycle (Verdant Pulse, 13s)
#   Q4: litter/veg   — Decomposition cycle (Verdant Pulse, 11s)
#
# 600s ground-state-init time averages (targets):
#   🦅 eagle    ~2.5%  (2–6%)    apex scarcity
#   🐇 rabbit  ~97.5%  (80–98%)  prey base
#   🐺 wolf    ~13.5%  (10–25%)  predator pack
#   🦌 deer    ~86.5%  (75–90%)  browsing herd
#   🌱 seedling ~18.6%  (15–35%)  active growth
#   🌲 tree    ~81.4%  (65–85%)  canopy
#   🍂 litter  ~25.7%  (15–35%)  decomposition
#   🌿 veg     ~74.3%  (65–85%)  ground cover
#
# Self-energy detunings (all large → populations near poles at ground state):
#   Q1 wolf/deer: Δ=1.65,  Q2 eagle/rabbit: Δ=2.25,  Q3 seed/tree: Δ=1.40
# Rabi timescales (wall-time at 0.5x sim-speed):
#   sun<->moon    50s  (driven at 0.04 Hz; Landau-Zener at dawn/dusk)
#   wolf<->deer   ~9s  (Rabi=0.420, Ω≈1.75, large detuning)
#   eagle<->rabbit ~30s (Rabi=0.200, Ω≈2.26, very large detuning)
#   seedling<->tree ~9s  (Rabi=0.500, Ω≈1.49)
#   litter<->veg   ~11s (Rabi=0.540)
#
# Cross-axis topology (13 couplings):
#   DAY chain:   sun -> seedling(Q3) -> rabbit <- eagle -> tree(Q3)
#   NIGHT chain: moon -> wolf -> rabbit, moon -> litter(Q4) -> seedling(Q3)
#   Trophic:     seedling -> rabbit, veg(Q4) -> deer, eagle -> tree
#   Predation:   wolf -> rabbit (secondary prey), deer -> veg, litter -> seedling
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

